# Pace — Changelog

> Historical record, newest first. Concise. Not required reading; open the relevant entry only. Apps Script versions = web-app deployment versions; Netlify IDs = deploy IDs.

## 2026-09-24 — Development operating system
- Canonical docs established: PACE_CONTEXT (current state), PACE_GUARDRAILS, PACE_DECISIONS, PACE_ARCHITECTURE, PACE_VALIDATION, PACE_ROADMAP, this changelog. Old monolithic PACE_CONTEXT backed up to `backups/PACE_CONTEXT.preOS.bak`; `README.md` and `docs/*.md` reduced to pointers (originals in `backups/*.preOS.bak`).
- No application code, production data or deployment changed. Suite 400/0.

## 2026-09-21 — Step 6: V2 production deployment (verification incomplete)
- Backend Apps Script v12 → **v13** (Steps 4–5.8 backend: balance snapshot `current_balance_covered`, anchor-day pace). Backend smoke 20/20; private profiles byte-identical to pre-deploy snapshot.
- Frontend `6ab012dc762d7bd31cd715fe` → **`6ab097334eab6fae293bd100`**; served files match local.
- Frontend smoke partial (Welcome, About, sign-in form, Guest Today, Guest add+undo OK); Guest edit/delete/reset, sheets, Money Plan render and post-deploy integrity re-check not done (interrupted).
- Rollback: v12 + `6ab012dc762d7bd31cd715fe`.

## 2026-09-21 — Step 5.8: Today slider + three spending states (local)
- Pace slider = today's spending vs today's pace; "left today"/"over today" labels; OVER PACE today-level status; "YOU SPENT A LOT TODAY." stamp via the large-expense rule; PROTECTED removed from Today; greeting boundaries 12/18h; `display_name` editable in Money Plan. Final acceptance audit READY; suite 400/0.
- (Before it: a full-screen "ledger" Today layout was tried and rejected; Today stays Pace-first.)

## 2026-09-20/21 — Step 5.5: balance semantics + paid/unpaid (local)
- Balance = snapshot of money available now; `current_balance_covered` records already-logged expense ids so they are not deducted again; anchor-day pace uses days after today. Commitment paid/unpaid toggle in Money Plan. 19 older expectations updated to the new semantics; +21 tests (R1–R21); 400/0.

## 2026-09-20 — Step 5: editable Current Balance in Money Plan (local)
- Balance field in Money Plan; only changed fields sent; balance-only edit = position save; unrelated edits never reset the anchor. +21 tests; 379/0.

## 2026-09-20 — Step 4: Today = presentation of `state.v2` (Netlify `6ab012dc762d7bd31cd715fe`)
- Engine was right; screen had mapped legacy fields. Main screen switched to V2 fields/states. Frontend only.

## 2026-09-20 — Money Model V2 Steps 1–3 (Apps Script v12, Netlify `6ab00a1dd3d6617cbc465293`)
- Step 1 V2 profile keys + `setup_state`; Step 1.5 commitments `{id,name,amount,status,paid_at}`; Step 2 pure engine `calculatePaceV2_` (balance anchor − expenses − savings − unpaid commitments); Step 3 onboarding + position setup. Private users started as `needs_position` (no invented balance).

## 2026-09-20 — Welcome + code-only sign-in (Apps Script v11 / Netlify `6aafb05db0540af6e23c1859`); Money Plan V1 (v10 / `6aafa42e8aa7ece91ab3cb27`)
- Profile-agnostic Welcome; login by code only. In-app income/savings/commitments editing.

## 2026-09-20 — Multi-user cutover (Apps Script v9, Netlify `6aaf2eb28aa7ecabc9b3cc78`)
- Access codes + signed sessions + per-profile tabs + Guest (Google OAuth abandoned). Legacy tabs kept as backups; 93 transactions preserved. Pre-cutover backup: `backups/prod_cutover_backup_20260920_061311.json` + Drive copy `1DsGzKcdoDPGyF5oc47pzNA6KGK40k9F36xR0Mt7xOgg`. Rollback-of-last-resort: v8 (`apps-script/Code.gs.v8.bak`).

## 2026-09-07 → 09-19 — MVP V1 (Apps Script v1–v8)
- Single-user sheet app; ledger UI chosen over dial; dynamic pace replaced fixed allowance; stable `transaction_id` + edit/delete/undo; optimistic UI; multi-currency display; device-local day (v8).
- Legacy V1 formula (superseded by V2, kept only as compatibility fields): `discretionary = income − savings − fixed`; `total_spendable = discretionary × period_days / days_in_month`; `today_pace = max(total_spendable − expenses_before_today, 0) / days_incl_today`; `remaining_pace = max(total_spendable − expenses_through_today, 0) / days_after_today`.
